What was removed from upstream
------------------------------

The donation strategy: its time slicing, its wallet, its endpoint, and the
code paths that switched mining to a developer pool. `donate-level` and
`donate-over-proxy` are still accepted so existing scripts do not break, then
ignored. `sudo ./oneclick.sh verify` greps the built binary for the upstream
endpoints and wallets and prints what it found; doc/ZERO_FEE.md explains the
method and what it can and cannot prove.

What is new here
----------------

The Zig miner, the installer, the proxy, the pool, the website, the pool
selection and anti-ban logic, and the documentation. Files created for ZMRIG
carry the same GPL-3.0 licence and are Copyright (C) 2026 @nggkhaiz.

